<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

Displays the completion status of a task that takes a while.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/progress)

<%= embed UI::ProgressPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Progress(value: 60) do
  ProgressLabel { "Uploading" }
  ProgressValue()
end
```

Progress tracks a task moving toward completion (an upload, an import, an install), unlike
[Meter](<%= page_path(:meter) %>), which shows a static measurement. Set `value:` from 0 to 100 (or pass
`min:` / `max:`). When you can't compute a percentage, reach for a [Loader](<%= page_path(:loader) %>) or
[Spinner](<%= page_path(:spinner) %>).

Two layouts via `variant:`: `:bar` (a horizontal track, the default) with the label and value above it, and
`:circular` (an SVG ring) with the value centered inside. Recolor the fill with `indicator_color:` and tune its
weight with `thickness:` (plus `size:` for the ring).

## Examples

### Circular

<%= embed UI::ProgressPreview, :circular %>

### Custom color & thickness

`indicator_color:` accepts any CSS color (a theme token like `var(--success-emphasis)` keeps it on-brand) and
`thickness:` the weight in pixels - for both the bar and the ring.

<%= embed UI::ProgressPreview, :custom %>

### File upload (controlled)

Advance the value as bytes arrive by setting `data-ui--progress-value-value` - the fill animates between
values, and at `max` every part gets `data-complete`, which the card uses (`group-has-data-complete:`) to swap
the icon and label and reveal an action.

<%= embed UI::ProgressPreview, :upload %>

```js
xhr.upload.addEventListener("progress", ({ loaded, total }) => {
  progress.setAttribute("data-ui--progress-value-value", Math.round((loaded / total) * 100))
})
```

From the server, replace it with a Turbo Stream as a job advances:

```ruby
turbo_stream.replace "import-progress", UI::Progress.new(value: import.percent, id: "import-progress", aria_label: "Import")
```

### RTL

The label and value swap sides and the bar fills from the right.

<%= embed UI::ProgressPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

The root exposes `data-variant` and one of `data-progressing`, `data-complete` or `data-indeterminate`
(also set on the label, value and track) for styling.

### Progress

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `value:` | `Numeric`, `nil` | - | Current value from `min:` to `max:`; `nil` is indeterminate. |
| `variant:` | `:bar`, `:circular` | `:bar` | Horizontal track or SVG ring. |
| `min:` | `Numeric` | `0` | Lower bound of the range. |
| `max:` | `Numeric` | `100` | Upper bound of the range. |
| `indicator_color:` | `String` (CSS color) | `var(--primary)` | Fill color, set as `--progress-color`. |
| `thickness:` | `Integer` (px) | `6` / `4` | Track weight: 6 for the bar, 4 for the ring. |
| `size:` | `Integer` (px) | `56` | Diameter of the ring (circular only). |
| `format:` | `Hash` (Intl.NumberFormat options) | percent | Formatting of the displayed value, as for Meter. |
| `locale:` | `String` | browser's | Locale for live updates. |
| `aria_label:` | `String` | - | Name the progress bar when there's no `ProgressLabel`. |

Other attributes go to the `role="progressbar"` root; `class:` is merged (set the bar width here).

### ProgressLabel

A `<span>` wired to the root with `aria-labelledby`.

### ProgressValue

A `<span>` with the formatted value; a block receives `|formatted, value|` to build the text yourself.

## Accessibility

- Progress renders `role="progressbar"` with `aria-valuenow`, `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax` and
  `aria-valuetext` reflecting the value.
- Give every progress bar a name - a `ProgressLabel` or `aria_label:` on the root.
- The circular SVG is `aria-hidden`; the accessible value comes from the root's ARIA attributes.
- The fill animation is disabled when the user prefers reduced motion.
